{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["C17"],
      "pins": ["C17.1", "C17.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C17-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C17 is a 0.1uF capacitor (libsource Device:C) but its footprint is 'Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder'. Pin 1 is on net 'unconnected-(C17-Pad1)' and pin 2 is on GND, so the capacitor is not connected to any supply rail.",
      "expected": "A decoupling capacitor should use a capacitor footprint and have both terminals connected to a circuit (e.g., a power rail and ground).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C17\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\") ... (libsource (lib \"Device\") (part \"C\") (description \"Unpolarized capacitor\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"unconnected-(C17-Pad1)\") ... (node (ref \"C17\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "C17 unconnected-_C17-Pad1_ 0 0.1u"}
      ],
      "impact": "The capacitor is electrically floating and provides no decoupling. The wrong footprint may also cause assembly problems if the part is placed.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["J3"],
      "pins": ["J3.1", "J3.2"],
      "nets": ["NET0041", "NET0025"],
      "observed": "J3 is a Conn_02x01 header. Pin 1 is on NET0041 (battery negative, U9.2, J5.3) and pin 2 is on NET0025 (BAT+). This places a 2-pin header directly across the 18650 battery.",
      "expected": "A power switch or jumper should be in series with the battery (e.g., between battery negative and GND), not directly across the cell, to avoid shorting it.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"J3\") (value \"Conn_02x01\") ...)"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"29\") (name \"NET0041\") ... (node (ref \"J3\") (pin \"1\") ...) (node (ref \"J5\") (pin \"3\") ...) (node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"2\") ...))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"19\") (name \"NET0025\") ... (node (ref \"J3\") (pin \"2\") ...) (node (ref \"J2\") (pin \"1\") ...) (node (ref \"J5\") (pin \"1\") ...) (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"1\") ...))"}
      ],
      "impact": "If a jumper or switch is installed on J3, it will short the battery, causing high current, potential damage, or fire.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U7"],
      "pins": ["U7.13", "U7.14"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "SKW92A pins 13 and 14 (LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX-) are both connected to the GND net.",
      "expected": "Unused Ethernet PHY outputs should not be tied directly to ground; they should be left floating or properly terminated.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") ...) (node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") ...))"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the Ethernet PHY is active, shorting its outputs to ground could damage the SKW92A. If the PHY is disabled, it may be harmless but is non-standard.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain clear anomalies: C17 is a floating capacitor with an inductor footprint, and J3 is a header wired directly across the battery, which would short the cell if jumpered. A third, lower-confidence issue is that two SKW92A Ethernet output pins are tied to ground."
}

